  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "Another week of significant activity, saw sixteen (16) units changing hands. Notably three (3) \nultramax deals setting new benchmarks: buyers spent $22 mill for eco type Crown 63 blt 2014 named \nHAKO; in a Japanese style bid, similarly aged Japanese built SANTA MARIA (61k blt 2014 \nImabari/Japan, eco type m/e) went for slightly less (region low $ 21 mill) but basis forward delivery \nbetween April - June next year. In an off-market deal, GRACE HARMONY (60k blt 2015 \nOnomichi/Japan) was committed for approximately $24 mill. Additionally, a rare animal, geared \npanamax bulker JAL KUMUD (76k blt 2008 Imabari/Japan Cr 4x30t) was acquired by Chinese \ninterests for just over $13 mill, establishing a new market benchmark.",
    "demolition": "All markets are stable (more or less) with NO reported sales in Subcontinent this week. \nFor an overview of demolition market rates, please check our comprehensive demometer below:"
  },
